          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Predicting What Comes Next: Exploring Sequences and Progressions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.844,
            0.068,
            0.883,
            0.084
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "179"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.108,
            0.776,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the first four terms of the sequence are 3, 6, 30, 870."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.152,
            0.51,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahānka–Fibonacci sequence"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.181,
            0.884,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A recursive rule or formula does not only have to involve the previous term — it could involve the previous two or more terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.22,
            0.884,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The most famous example of such a sequence is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "V _ { 1 } ,   V _ { 2 } ,   V _ { 3 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " … where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "V_{1}=1,V_{2}=2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "V_{_n} = V_{_{n-1}} + V_{_{n-2}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We compute:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.4,
            0.264,
            0.637,
            0.287
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "V_{3}=V_{2}+V_{1}=2+1=3"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.4,
            0.288,
            0.636,
            0.311
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "V_{4}=V_{3}+V_{2}=3+2=5"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.313,
            0.637,
            0.337
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "V_{5}=V_{4}+V_{3}=5+3=8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.334,
            0.37,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So we get the sequence"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.359,
            0.646,
            0.378
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "1 , 2 , 3 , 5 , 8 , 1 3 , 2 1 , 3 4 , \\ldots"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.383,
            0.732,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "where each term is obtained by adding the previous two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.407,
            0.708,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you write the next two terms of this sequence?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.43,
            0.886,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you recognise this sequence from previous grades? That’s right, it is the Virahānka–Fibonacci sequence! It was first written down explicitly and studied by Virahānka in his work Vṛttajātisamuchaya in the 7th century CE. He discovered it in the context of Prakrit meter and poetry! It was further studied by the linguist-mathematicians Gopāla (c. 1135 CE) and Hemachandra (c. 1150 CE). The sequence was later also studied by the Italian mathematician Fibonacci (c. 1200 CE)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.571,
            0.886,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Virahānka sequence plays an important role throughout mathematics and science. We will encounter it again many times in later grades."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.648,
            0.621,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 8.1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.699,
            0.883,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the first five terms of the sequence in which the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is given by (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t_{n} = 3n - 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { n } = 2 - 5 n"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { n } = n ^ { 2 } - 2 n + 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.742,
            0.847,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 5 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " terms of the sequence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { n } = 5 n - 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.766,
            0.884,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Determine whether 97 and 172 are terms of the sequence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { n } = 5 n - 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.808,
            0.759,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Which term of the sequence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { n } = 5 n - 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is 607?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.832,
            0.885,
            0.891
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. A sequence is given by the recursive rule "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t_{1} = - 5, t_{n + 1} = t_{n} + 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the first five terms of the sequence. Is 52 a term of this sequence? If so, which term is it?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
